  "semanticReview": [
    "Spring milestone and release-candidate states remain separate from stable releases; limited Boot coverage is preserved rather than certifying every project in a roundup.",
    "Spring Boot 4.1.0/4.0.7 and Spring AI 2.0.0 baseline versions 4.0/4.1/7.0 are unchanged.",
    "Spring Security release versions and ended open-source support generations are retained as historical information, with commercial support separate.",
    "Argo CD pre-release mTLS and Source Integrity configuration are not made default enforcement or first-introduction claims.",
    "Kubernetes Stable maturity is not translated as automatic enablement on all clusters.",
    "TeamCity requires prior authentication; affected versions through 2025.11.4 and fixed 2026.1 remain separate from the unaffected Cloud offering.",
    "NetScaler patching, alternate origin bypass and DTLS listeners retain distinct scopes; Access remains a product name.",
    "WAF numeric maximum 3, Log/Block actions and absence of custom response-body rules are preserved.",
    "Security Overview domain-level launch and account-level roadmap are not collapsed into released account-wide availability.",
    "Dynatrace historical GitHub Enterprise Cloud availability is not extended to every plan.",
    "GitHub risk assessment scope and reported findings are not made a complete security audit.",
    "BadHost affected interval >= 0.8.3 and < 1.0.1, patched 1.0.1, application conditions and both proxy/header-trust mitigation prerequisites are retained.",
    "eMudhra historical cloudflared version 2026.10.2 is not called the latest version; SDK updates and trust policy remain separate and disabling verification is rejected.",
    "CNCF free project access, named adoption list and absence of independent vulnerability-removal proof remain distinct.",
    "Formal usted imperatives follow existing Spanish batches; titles, negation, conditionals, identifiers and target-language flow were reread. Internal reviewFocus remains private."
  ],
